# Pipecat agent stack — Kubernetes environment template.
#
# This is the k8s counterpart to .env.example (which targets the docker-compose
# / VM deploy). It exists because two things differ in Kubernetes:
#
#   1. Per-node IPs are auto-detected, NOT set here. The detect-ip initContainer
#      discovers each node's public IP at startup. Setting EXT_IP_ADDRESS /
#      SIPBRIDGE_SIP_SIGNAL_IP / SIPBRIDGE_MEDIA_IP here (or in the bundle) would
#      OVERRIDE that per-node value and make every node advertise the same wrong
#      address in SDP — i.e. broken/one-way audio. They are deliberately absent.
#
#   2. There is no host.docker.internal. The worker and the SIP gateway run as
#      containers in ONE hostNetwork DaemonSet pod, so they share the host's
#      network namespace and reach each other on 127.0.0.1 — exactly like the
#      compose `network_mode: host` setup. The loopback URLs below are therefore
#      correct as-is; do NOT change them to Service DNS unless you split the
#      worker and gateway into separate pods (not the shipped topology).
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
# --------------------
# Non-secret config (the URLs/ports below) normally lives in the ConfigMap
# (deploy/k8s/base/configmap.yaml) and you don't need to repeat it. This file's
# primary job is to be the *source for the secretenv bundle*: copy it, fill in
# the secrets, and feed it to the publisher:
#
#     cp agents/pipecat/.env.example.k8s agents/pipecat/deploy/k8s/.env.staging
#     # edit .env.staging — fill in the SECRETS section
#     cd agents/pipecat/deploy/k8s
#     ../bundle-secretenv.sh --env=staging        # -> Secret pipecat-secretenv
#
# Anything you leave in the bundle OVERRIDES the ConfigMap at container start
# (the native loaders use Object.assign semantics). So: bundle secrets, and only
# include a config URL here if you intend to override the ConfigMap default.


# ============================================================================
# SECRETS — bundle these (or put them in the pipecat-secrets Secret instead)
# ============================================================================

# Shared with lib/handlers/pipecat.js on the llm-agent server side — must match.
PIPECAT_DISPATCH_TOKEN=change-me-dispatch
PIPECAT_JOIN_SECRET=change-me-join
# x-shared-token header value for the llm-agent agent-db API — must match server.
SHARED_API_TOKEN=change-me-shared

# Outbound-trunk SIP digest creds (sipbridge + FreeSWITCH). Leave blank if the
# SBC authenticates outbound by source-IP allowlist rather than digest.
PIPECAT_SIP_USERNAME=
PIPECAT_SIP_PASSWORD=

# sipbridge REST control-API bearer (worker <-> sipbridge, loopback).
SIPBRIDGE_API_TOKEN=change-me-sipbridge

# FreeSWITCH ingress secrets.
ESL_SECRET=change-me-esl
CALL_API_TOKEN=change-me-call-api
WORKER_EVENT_TOKEN=change-me-call-api   # default: same as CALL_API_TOKEN
ESL_POLLER_TOKEN=change-me-call-api     # = CALL_API_TOKEN

# Voiceblender ingress secrets.
VOICEBLENDER_API_KEY=change-me-vb
VOICEBLENDER_VSI_TOKEN=

# Model / provider API keys — set the ones you use.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ULTRAVOX_API_KEY=


# ============================================================================
# CONFIG — already set in the ConfigMap; uncomment here only to override
# ============================================================================
#
# These loopback URLs are CORRECT for Kubernetes: the worker (:8082) and every
# gateway share one hostNetwork pod, so 127.0.0.1 is the same loopback for all
# of them. They mirror deploy/k8s/base/configmap.yaml.

# --- worker <-> FreeSWITCH + esl-poller (all 127.0.0.1, same pod) ---
# PIPECAT_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8082/freeswitch/audio
# WORKER_EVENT_WEBHOOK=http://127.0.0.1:8082/freeswitch/events
# ESL_POLLER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4001

# --- worker <-> sipbridge (same pod) ---
# SIPBRIDGE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
# SIPBRIDGE_WORKER_WS_BASE=ws://127.0.0.1:8082

# --- worker <-> voiceblender (same pod) ---
# VOICEBLENDER_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# VOICEBLENDER_WORKER_WS_BASE=ws://127.0.0.1:8082

# --- outbound trunk host (non-secret half; creds are in SECRETS above) ---
# PIPECAT_SIP_OUTBOUND=sbc.aplisay.example:5061;transport=tls
# PIPECAT_SIP_FROM_DOMAIN=pipecat.sbc.aplisay.example

# llm-agent REST surface. This is the ONE URL that is genuinely topology-
# dependent:
#   - llm-agent OUTSIDE the cluster -> use its public HTTPS URL (as below).
#   - llm-agent INSIDE the cluster  -> use its in-cluster Service DNS, e.g.
#     http://llm-agent.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local:<port>
# SERVICE_BASE_URI=https://api.aplisay.example

# LOGLEVEL=info


# ============================================================================
# DO NOT SET IN KUBERNETES — auto-detected per node by the detect-ip initContainer
# ============================================================================
# Setting any of these (here or in the bundle) overrides the per-node detected
# public IP and breaks RTP media. Listed only as a warning.
#   EXT_IP_ADDRESS
#   SIPBRIDGE_SIP_SIGNAL_IP
#   SIPBRIDGE_MEDIA_IP
